WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.369
-Ladies and gentlemen,
it is time for "Bad Signs."

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:04.603
Here we go.

00:00:04.603 --> 00:00:08.741
-♪ Ain't we lucky we got 'em? ♪

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:15.448
♪ Bad signs ♪

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:19.285
-Now, these are pictures of
funny or weird signs

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.187
that you saw and sent in to us.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.422
But these are all real signs.

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.524
This first one was
sent in by Jackie Avery

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:25.925
in Holliston, Massachusetts.

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.426
Hey, we love Massachusetts.

00:00:27.426 --> 00:00:30.362
She was trying to find a quiet
place to eat her lunch at work.

00:00:30.362 --> 00:00:31.397
-Oh, okay.

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:33.065
-Yeah, and spotted
this sign here.

00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:34.634
It says...

00:00:40.072 --> 00:00:41.141
-There you go.

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:42.509
-Could have just said,
"It's closed."

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:43.909
Yeah.

00:00:43.909 --> 00:00:47.446
This next one was sent in by
Bob Riggins in Boise, Idaho.

00:00:47.446 --> 00:00:51.283
He spotted this great deal
at his local gas station here.

00:00:51.283 --> 00:00:53.086
It says...

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:59.792
It's not bad.
-That's not bad -- just 10%.

00:00:59.792 --> 00:01:03.830
-It's only 10%. Yeah.
-90% good.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.597
-This next one is from
Robin Rosenthal

00:01:05.597 --> 00:01:06.666
in Stamford, Connecticut.

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:07.734
Stamford!
-Yeah.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.235
-Hey, what's up?

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.704
She was shopping for
some Halloween decorations

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:12.705
and spotted this.

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.874
I think this is funny.

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:17.944
It says, yeah,
real skull is $3.94

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:21.314
Faux skulls are also $3.94.

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:23.883
-I want to get the real skulls.

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:25.117
-No, no,
you want the faux skulls.

00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:26.319
-The faux one?
-Yeah, they're the same price.

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:27.553
-Yeah.

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:28.788
-This one lasts you longer
than the real skull.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:30.556
-Yeah, 'cause the real one
will deteriorate

00:01:30.556 --> 00:01:31.891
'cause it's real.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:32.959
-This one's for, like,
"Hamlet" or something like that,

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:34.193
if you're doing Shakespeare.

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:35.394
-Yeah, this one's for, like,
goofy kids' stuff.

00:01:35.394 --> 00:01:37.329
-Yeah, then you put, like,
candy in this one.

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:39.131
Look, it's selling more
than the real skulls.

00:01:39.131 --> 00:01:40.799
-Right. It's almost all gone.

00:01:40.799 --> 00:01:42.235
It's a real human skull
in there.

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:46.172
-This next one is
from Jason Riley

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:47.439
in Anaheim, California.

00:01:47.439 --> 00:01:51.177
He spotted this while driving.
It says...

00:01:52.778 --> 00:01:54.581
That's not bad.

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:58.751
That's the best kind of massage.
-I love the crawfish massage.

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:01.020
-I "gar-on-tee" it?

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:04.157
-Yeah, I "gar-on-tee"
it's cold and dry.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:05.524
No, it's hot and juicy.

00:02:05.524 --> 00:02:08.694
-This next one is from
Ruby Jones in Phoenix.

00:02:08.694 --> 00:02:10.096
That's a good name.
-Yeah, Ruby Jones.

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:11.630
-Ruby Jones.
Phoenix, Arizona.

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:13.766
She parked her car in
a parking garage

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:16.803
and was trying to find a way out
and she found -- Look at this.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:18.671
"Elevator."
-Well, close.

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:19.839
-Yeah.

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:21.607
Close enough.
-Yeah, Close enough. Stairs.

00:02:21.607 --> 00:02:23.008
-Close enough.
Stairs, elevator.

00:02:23.008 --> 00:02:24.544
What's the big deal?
-Want a skull?

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:26.946
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:28.748
-This next one is from
Joe Collins

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.316
in Biloxi, Mississippi.

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:33.986
He was out for a walk
and spotted this sign here.

00:02:33.986 --> 00:02:36.723
It says -- Can we zoom in on
the sign there?

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:38.224
"Invisible fence."

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.692
-Oh.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:44.197
-Looks pretty visible to me,
but I'm glad the sign is there.

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:46.699
-It will fool the dog.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:49.635
-This next one is from
Beth Jackson in Washington, D.C.

00:02:49.635 --> 00:02:53.973
She was going to pick something
up and spotted this sign here.

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:01.281
-Hmm.
-How do you even find this sign?

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:05.251
-Yeah. That had should be
special-made, right?

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:07.119
Nobody has that sign in stock.

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:08.888
-It looks like --
Yeah, no one made this.

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:09.922
This is a sign
you can buy from a --

00:03:09.922 --> 00:03:11.023
-I need a sign that says,

00:03:11.023 --> 00:03:13.492
"The front door
is around the back door."

00:03:13.492 --> 00:03:16.328
-Yeah.
No, the back door is the front.

00:03:16.328 --> 00:03:17.696
Oh. This is the back door.

00:03:17.696 --> 00:03:20.066
The front door
is around the back.

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:22.268
There's an invisible fence,
so just be careful.

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:23.703
-I can't see the fen-- Oh, wait.
It's right there.

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:27.306
-Oh, there's a floating sign
that says, "Invisible fence."

00:03:27.306 --> 00:03:29.842
What is it -- Is this floating?

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:32.311
-Wait. There's a fence here?
-Oh, this one's awesome.

00:03:32.311 --> 00:03:33.980
This is great.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.848
I always like looking at
the technology,

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.283
new toilet technology.

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:38.651
-You love new toilet technology.
-That's right.

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:41.621
This is from Cindy Klein in
Naperville, Illinois.

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:43.589
She was shopping for
a toilet in Home Depot

00:03:43.589 --> 00:03:44.590
and saw this sign.

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.792
Look at this.

00:03:46.792 --> 00:03:51.230
It says, "Flushes 7 billiard
balls in a single flush."

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:54.701
What situation...

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:56.535
-Six?

00:03:56.535 --> 00:03:57.937
-[ Shouting indistinctly ]

00:03:57.937 --> 00:03:59.739
The boss can't find out!

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:01.573
-[ Gulping ]

00:04:01.573 --> 00:04:02.608
Swallow all these
billiard balls!

00:04:02.608 --> 00:04:04.243
-Don't swallow
the billiard balls!

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:05.611
Flush them!

00:04:05.611 --> 00:04:08.947
-I got to swallow seven of them!
No toilet can handle that!

00:04:08.947 --> 00:04:11.184
-What are we gonna do with
the cue ball?!

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.220
Can't handle the cue ball.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.487
-Yeah, can't get the
8 ball either.

00:04:15.487 --> 00:04:18.124
-No.
-It's only seven.

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:19.592
-That's true.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:21.527
[ Cymbal crash ]

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:22.762
-It flushes
seven billiard balls.

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:23.796
-Yeah, seven billiard balls.

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:25.531
-You got to choose
which one, man.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:27.266
-Yeah, 13 ball? I don't know.

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:28.968
-It's that "Squid Game," dude.

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.102
-Stripes, solids,

00:04:30.102 --> 00:04:31.437
whatever you want.

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:32.839
You better hope it's a solid.
-Yeah.

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:34.640
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:41.814
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:44.917
-Oh, man, I ate a billiard ball.
I feel like an idiot.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:45.952
-No.

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:48.086
-Yeah, I ate seven of them.

00:04:48.086 --> 00:04:51.390
-Alright, now you should
feel like an idiot, maybe.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:53.126
What is the first number ball
that came out?

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:55.828
-Oh, let's see. Oh, lottery!

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:57.596
Number 6!

00:04:57.596 --> 00:04:59.665
[ Popping ]
-Number 2! Hey!

00:04:59.665 --> 00:05:01.534
-Number 2 came out.

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:05.738
-It's a lottery.

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:07.974
-[ Popping ]

00:05:07.974 --> 00:05:10.977
7, 6, 49.

00:05:10.977 --> 00:05:12.812
-Don't touch it! Don't touch it!

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:15.114
-53. Sorry.

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:17.150
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.618 --> 00:05:21.420
-It's an 8.
-Oh, sorry.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:24.790
-I apologize. It's a 3.
-Yeah.

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:26.292
-I know. Sorry. I went too far.

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:27.627
-Awful.
-Went too far.

00:05:27.627 --> 00:05:29.328
That's disgusting.
-Awful.

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:31.130
-Awful type of humor.
-Awful.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.799
-I apologize.
That is beneath me.

00:05:33.799 --> 00:05:36.769
-Oh, my gosh. And above you.
-And above me, as well.

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:42.041
Last one is from Rodney Ames
in White Plains, New York.

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:43.443
He stopped at his
favorite coffee shop

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:46.512
to get some lunch
and saw this in the window.

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:48.447
"Open daily.
Closed Tuesdays."

00:05:48.447 --> 00:05:49.581
There you go.

00:05:49.581 --> 00:05:51.484
That's all the time
we have for "Bad Signs."

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:53.285
If you see a funny sign,
e-mail it to us at

00:05:53.285 --> 00:05:55.254
badsigns@tonightshow.com.

